WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.300
And Examer Lasers cut Lasix per eye hardware and energy costs to tens of dollars by replacing

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.480
diamond blades with micrometer scale UV ablation.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:12.680
This is First Principles Daily, episode 109.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:18.880
Surgeons once corrected vision by making precise radial cuts in the cornea, with gem quality

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:19.680
diamond blades.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.100
Each incision was guided by hand and limited by the blade's edge.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:31.560
XMR lasers later replaced that approach with pulses of 193 nanometer ultraviolet light that

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.800
removed corneal tissue 1 micrometer at a time without heating the surrounding cells.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:43.160
The shift moved the dominant cost from expensive single use blades and operating room time to

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.820
the amortized price of a pulsed gas laser.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.320
Its raw consumables per eye now sit in the low tens of dollars.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.420
That change rested on recognizing that the physical requirement was controlled removal

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.480
of collagen layers rather than mechanical slicing.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.400
The question became how to deliver energy that broke molecular bonds directly.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:09.520
Radial carototomy treated myopia by placing a set number of radial incisions that allowed

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.320
the cornea to flatten under intraocular pressure.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.440
The technique copied the logic of earlier manual eye surgery.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:21.780
A skilled hand guided a sharp instrument whose geometry had been perfected over decades.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.760
Diamond blades were the accepted standard because they held an edge longer than steel

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.380
and produced cleaner cuts than any alternative than available.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.820
Each blade cost hundreds of dollars, each required sterilization between cases.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.600
Each still risked irregular depth that could induce astigmatism or glare.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:46.320
Operating rooms therefore treated the blade as a high-value consumable, whose price was

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.820
accepted as an unavoidable part of the procedure.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.100
No one questioned the underlying assumption that tissue removal had to occur through mechanical

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.360
slicing rather than direct molecular bond breaking.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.380
That assumption locked the cost structure around the price of diamonds.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.360
The time needed for manual marking and the risk margin built into every case.

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:12.680
The XMR approach began by asking what physical process could remove corneal collagen without

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.900
mechanical contact or thermal damage.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:22.400
researches identified that 193 nanometer photons from an argon fluoride laser could break carbon

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.460
nitrogen bonds in the tissue. The photons ejected fragments in a photochemical plume while

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:34.740
leaving adjacent cells intact. Once that mechanism was established, the engineering task became

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:41.200
delivering controlled pulses whose energy density sat just above the ablation threshold. Early

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:47.400
systems required large water-cooled lasers and complex beam delivery optics. The core physics

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:53.820
remained unchanged. Photon energy matched molecular bond strength. Over successive generations,

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.980
manufacturers replaced custom gas handling assemblies with standardized modules.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.020
Commodity prices fell as semiconductor lithography adopted the same wavelength.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:10.440
The magic wand estimate for the materials consumed per eye centers on a few liters of argon

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.420
fluoride gas mixture, plus the electricity for a few hundred pulses.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:21.080
At current industrial gas prices, those inputs total roughly 20-40 dollars, once the laser

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.260
is already installed.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:28.240
The older blade-based idiot index was high because the finished procedure price incorporated

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:33.400
hundreds of dollars in single-use diamond tooling, plus the labor of manual alignment.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:39.760
Each redesign step that reduced optical component count or lengthened gas fill lifetime would

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.180
or directly lowered that ratio.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:46.980
The steps attacked the manufactured subsystems rather than the raw photons or the corneal

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:47.800
tissue itself.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:53.140
Trade-offs included the need for precise eye tracking to keep the beam registered during

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.480
the few seconds of ablation.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:04:01.020
The corneal flaps still had to be created mechanically or with a femtosecond laser before the eczema

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:01.360
step.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.980
Both remained separate cost centers.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:11.820
One consolidation moved from discrete high-voltage power supplies and separate cooling loops to integrated solid state drivers.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:16.320
Those drivers reused waste heat within the gas recirculation path.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.220
They cut both mass and maintenance hours.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:26.660
Another move standardized the beam delivery arm from custom machine titanium mounts to cast aluminum assemblies.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.900
Tolerances could be held by the same CNC processes used for industrial scanners.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:37.220
A third move lengthened the interval between gas refills by improving the purity of the

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.380
recirculation filters.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.620
The same fill now supports several hundred more procedures before the fluoride concentration

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.600
drops below the ablation threshold.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:51.680
Each of these changes addressed a specific manufactured intermediary rather than the fundamental

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.320
photon tissue interaction.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:59.440
The interaction had already reached its physical limit once the 193 nanometer wavelength was

00:04:59.440 --> 00:04:59.820
chosen.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:06.020
Once examer sources became standardized, the per procedure hardware and energy costs settled

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.820
in the range of tens of dollars for high volume centers.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:13.900
That marked a clear reduction from the hundreds previously spent on blades and setup.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:18.480
The new idiot index for the light delivery portion itself is now low.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:24.620
The dominant remaining expenses sit in the flap creation step, regulatory compliance and

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:27.360
clinic overhead rather than in the ablation materials.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:33.580
Limits persist around the initial capital cost of the laser platform. Limits also persist

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:38.800
around the need for a sterile field and the biological variability of individual cornyas

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.820
that still requires surgeon oversight. The photochemical process itself has reached

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:49.080
close to its physical floor. Further gains would require commoditizing the entire delivery

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:53.220
system or shifting flap creation to the same non-contact method.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:58.960
Reported outcomes show that the precision of depth control improved from roughly 50 micrometer

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.020
variability with blades to single micrometer steps with the laser.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:08.380
Capital recovery and regulatory overhead still dominate the overall procedure price.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:13.560
A corneal surface whose shape is adjusted by counting photons instead of counting blade

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:19.040
strokes shows that the cost driver often hides inside the assumed method of material removal.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:25.160
The same principle applies whenever a consumable tool can be replaced by a tunable energy source

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:29.300
whose price scales with usage rather than with each individual part.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:35.700
Which other manual tissue shaping procedures still carry high idiot indexes simply because

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.120
no one has yet matched the photon energy to the molecular bond?

